[[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3238633\">7010A04</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238652\">7010C54</a></p><p>1. Disconnect the rod (1a) from the guide spring (1b)</p><p>2. Disconnect the linkage from the lock and save it.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019012.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the link is undamaged.</p><p>1. Replace the rod retaining bush.</p><p>2. Connect the linkage to the lock.</p><p>3.  Connect the rod to the guide spring.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2019013.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3238652\">7010C54</a></p><p><a href=\"#/3238633\">7010A04</a></p>"]]